      "document": {
        "resourceId": "fixture-ip1-f07",
        "sourceVersionId": "fixture-ip1-f07-v1",
        "title": "Branch integration budget",
        "titleKo": "",
        "format": "html",
        "extractorVersion": "structured-v2-compatible-fixture",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "fixture-ip1-f07-h",
            "order": 0,
            "kind": "heading",
            "text": "Timing of shared operating costs",
            "metadata": {
              "schemaVersion": 1,
              "level": 2,
              "links": []
            },
            "textSha256": "4237275bb55ccd388bf9737674a4f43edf398b01e6e3bc31c97a0964f7e0675d"
          },
          {
            "id": "fixture-ip1-f07-b",
            "order": 1,
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Two branches will combine their records in a planned integration. Their overhead consists of shared rent and administrative salaries; those costs are required to operate the branches.",
            "metadata": {
              "schemaVersion": 1,
              "links": []
            },
            "textSha256": "2613ba7debf64c4b3ec3a3d6303d29083305f62617064d80d45236ea2d468aa8"
          },
          {
            "id": "fixture-ip1-f07-t",
            "order": 2,
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "The budget assumes that overhead will decline after the integration of the two branches. This timing assumption applies to the shared operating costs, not to the equity raised to finance the project. The forecast does not describe the overhead as unnecessary spending. Keep the timing assumption separate from the question of how the project is financed.",
            "metadata": {
              "schemaVersion": 1,
              "links": []
            },
            "textSha256": "4591e9eea1bd3d17c06e96f8a246097a0209a94d1eddb301335f26546f551d68"
          },
          {
            "id": "fixture-ip1-f07-a",
            "order": 3,
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "The financing schedule records new ordinary shares issued to investors. It does not change the operating-cost assumption.",
            "metadata": {
              "schemaVersion": 1,
              "links": []
            },
            "textSha256": "b0bde0f42c327818299db42e86243a30f40a58c1821098c406e4080fa12ecfbe"
          }
        ]
      },
      "targetBlockId": "fixture-ip1-f07-t"
    },
